  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HYDROLOGICAL RESTORATION OF KEY WETLANDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Located in the Gulf of Mexico, the Alvarado Lagoon System is important for waterfowl, waterbirds, wading birds, shorebirds and landbirds such as Snowy Plover, Red Knot, and Buff-breasted Sandpiper. This project will restore 10,047.3 acres of wetlands by removing sediment, redirecting wastewater, and reseeding mangroves. It will protect 1,729.7 acres of wetlands through the creation of Private Conservation Areas or Municipal Ecological Reserves. It will also provide training and environmental education for teachers and children.</narrative>
  </description>
